 ### SDR output options
 
+Choose **ADALM-Pluto** to configure a libiio device URI, Python executable, TX
+gain and timeout. Shared RF settings set the sample rate, centre frequency and
+filter bandwidth for Pluto. HackRF VGA/amp controls apply only to HackRF.
+See [Pluto setup](docs/PLUTO.md) for dependencies and known test limitations.
+
 | Output | Description |
 |---|---|
 | **HackRF** (default) | Transmit via a connected HackRF One. Uses the TX VGA gain and amp settings above. |
+| **ADALM-Pluto** | Transmit fresh non-cyclic IQ buffers through pyadi-iio/libiio; supports explicit IP/USB device URIs. |
 | **IQ File** | Write raw signed 8-bit interleaved IQ samples to a binary file (`[I0, Q0, I1, Q1, …]`). |
 | **UDP stream** | Stream IQ bytes to a UDP destination (e.g. `127.0.0.1:4567`). Packets are 32 768 bytes. |
 | **TCP server** | Open a TCP server on the specified port. The app waits for a client, then streams IQ bytes continuously. |
